d. assist in the process of submitting an application for the determination of Protection.

Article 22

The Regional Government is responsible for efforts to protect Women and Children from acts of Violence that occur in the form of:

a. physical Violence;
b. sexual Violence;
c. economic Violence;
d. social Violence;
e. psychological Violence;
f. domestic neglect;
g. coercion or deprivation of freedom; and
h. threats of certain acts.

Article 1

In this Regional Regulation, what is meant by:

Region is North Lombok Regency;

Regional Government is the Regent and Regional Apparatus as elements of the Regional Government administration;

Regent is the Regent of North Lombok;

Regional Apparatus Work Unit, hereinafter abbreviated as SKPD, is the Regional Apparatus Work Unit within the North Lombok Regency Government;

Implementation of Protection is all actions and service efforts to guarantee and protect the rights of Women and Children organized by the Regional Government and Society;

Child is a person who has not reached 18 (eighteen) years of age, including a Child still in the womb; Service is immediate activities and actions carried out by Professional personnel in accordance with their respective professions in the form of counseling, therapy and advocacy for empowerment and recovery;

Assistance is activities and actions carried out by an Assistant during the service process; Assistant is a person or representative from an Institution who has expertise in providing Assistance/social worker who has professional competence in their field;

Institution is a community non-governmental organization (NGO) that provides Assistance;

Supervision is the process of monitoring activities carried out systematically on the entire Implementation of Protection of legal aid for Children and Women;

Society is individuals, families, groups, social organizations and/or community organizations; Regional Revenue and Expenditure Budget, hereinafter abbreviated as APBD, is the annual financial plan of the Region established by Regional Regulation;

Integrated Service Center for Women and Children Empowerment, hereinafter abbreviated as P2TP2A, is an empowerment and Protection service for Women and Children established by the Government that is community-based;

Violence is any act against a Child that results in misery or suffering physically, psychologically, sexually, and/or neglect, including threats to commit acts, coercion, or deprivation of liberty unlawfully;

Women victims of Violence are Women who experience actions that result in misery or suffering physically, sexually, economically or psychologically, including threats of certain actions, coercion or deprivation of liberty arbitrarily, whether occurring in the public sphere or in private life;

Children victims of Violence are Children who experience actions that result in misery or suffering physically, mentally, sexually, psychologically or neglect that threatens life, body and degrades human dignity;

Children in emergency situations as referred to are Children who become refugees, Children victims of riots and turmoil, Children victims of disasters and Children in conflict situations;

Children in disaster situations are natural disasters, fire disasters and riots;

Handling of complaints is a series of actions taken by integrated service providers to follow up on reports of acts of Violence against Women and Children submitted by victims, families or Society;

Social rehabilitation is services aimed at restoring and developing the ability of a person experiencing social dysfunction to be able to carry out social functions normally;

Social reintegration is an effort to reunite victims with family members, substitute families, or Society that can provide Protection and fulfill the needs of victims;

Integrated service unit or abbreviated as UPT is a unit that performs an integrated service function for Women and Children victims of Violence;

Safe house is a temporary shelter that aims to provide Protection and a sense of security to victims of Violence;

Child Protection Institution or abbreviated as LPA is an Independent Institution in the field of Child Protection and fulfillment of Children's rights that is community-based;

North Lombok Regency Integrated Service Center or abbreviated as PPT KLU is a form of integrated service implementation based on community health centers to handle victims of Violence against Women and Children which includes medical, medicolegal, and psychosocial services.

Article 24

(1) The Regional Government conducts prevention of Violence against Women and Children by means of:

a. socializing laws and regulations;
b. providing counseling/guidance;
c. providing education on the dangers of domestic Violence;
d. conducting seminars/workshops or the like;
e. forming work networks in efforts to prevent Violence;
f. conducting coordination, integration, synchronization of Violence prevention based on partnership patterns;
g. forming a Violence prevention system, mapping of locations or areas prone to the occurrence of Violence; and
h. increasing Society's awareness in behaving in accordance with religious norms and morality.
(2) In addition to the Regional Government, prevention as referred to in paragraph (1) must be implemented by:
a. family and/or closest relatives;
b. Society;
c. educational institutions;
d. health institutions;
e. social community institutions; and
f. the business world and other institutions.

Article 14

(1) The relevant SKPD responsible for the Protection of Women and Children shall organize prevention and Protection in the form of:

a. dissemination of information;
b. developing data centers;
c. organizing education on the prevention of Violence against Women and Children;
d. developing child-friendly school models;
e. encouraging increased participation of Children in preventing Violence against Children as well as socialization and promotion of Children's rights through the establishment of Children's Forums/Children's Councils.
f. preparing a code of ethics for educators and orphanage officers as well as parties involved in handling Children;
g. providing guidelines or SOPs on handling Violence against Children;
h. preparing guidelines for the implementation of recovery and social Reintegration for Child victims of Violence;
i. preparing guidelines for the participation of the Community in providing recovery and Reintegration services;
j. involving the participation of the Community in recovery and Reintegration services for Child victims of Violence;
k. raising awareness about safe sex, the dangers of cigarettes, alcohol, narcotics and psychotropic substance abuse, child marriage, pornography, pornographic acts and HIV/AIDS to families, Communities and Children;
l. enhancing the capacity of families and Child care Institutions regarding Child Protection and child-rearing skills.
m. enhancing the capacity of all Child Protection services;
n. guarantee of continuity of character education in accordance with the 12 (twelve) year compulsory education program;
o. fulfillment of the right to legal identity for Children and Women including birth certificates and marriage certificates;
p. guarantee of obtaining standard health services;
q. guarantee of the right of Children to receive exclusive breastfeeding with the obligation of public spaces to provide breastfeeding corners;
r. guarantee of Protection and fulfillment of Children's rights from the womb and Women's rights;
s. fulfillment of Children's needs in accordance with the age of the Child;
t. Assistance and reproductive and psychological health services for adolescent Children and Women;
u. development of a Marriage Age Maturity Program;
v. strengthening the function of non-governmental Institutions or organizations engaged in Child empowerment; and
w. encouraging and facilitating the development of Child-Friendly Districts.
(2) Implementation of prevention as referred to in paragraph (1) may cooperate with Educational Institutions, Religious Institutions, Media, Business Entities and/or NGOs.

Article 17

(1) The relevant SKPD responsible for social affairs and Protection of Women and Children shall organize Rehabilitation, Reintegration and Empowerment in the form of:

a. Assistance for Women and Child victims;
b. provision of Safe houses;
c. healing or recovery;
d. return to family and Community;
e. facilitating the development of interests and talents for Women and Children;
f. developing economic ventures for adult Women;
g. developing creative spaces for Children; and
h. conducting Supervision, monitoring and evaluation of the Rehabilitation, Reintegration and Empowerment process.
(2) Implementation of Rehabilitation, Reintegration and Empowerment as referred to in paragraph (1) letters a through d may cooperate with educational Institutions, Rehabilitation facilities, Safe houses, private Institutions and/or NGOs.
(3) The mechanism for Organizing Protection against Violence towards Women and Children shall be organized according to Standard Operating Procedures (SOP) and Service Standards (SP) which will be further regulated by Regent Regulation.

Article 26

(1) The Regional Government implements Integrated Services for Women and Children victims of acts of Violence through activities:

a. complaint services;
b. health services;
c. counseling;
d. spiritual guidance;
e. social Rehabilitation services;
f. legal assistance and Accompaniment services; and/or
g. repatriation and Reintegration.
(2) Services as referred to in paragraph (1) must be supported by facilities in the form of:
a. special service rooms within the police force;
b. expert and professional personnel;
c. service centers and safe houses; and/or
d. other facilities and infrastructure needed for victim recovery.
(3) The implementation of Services for victims of acts of Violence is carried out in an integrated manner by the Regional Government together with P2TP2A with other social institutions.
(4) P2TP2A and other social institutions as referred to in paragraph (3) may receive and send case referrals from other service units in a networked manner.
(5) Integrated Services for victims of acts of Violence as referred to in paragraphs (1) through (4) are implemented in accordance with Standard Operating Procedures.

Article 13

Implementation of Protection of Women and Children includes:

a. prevention and Protection;
b. Handling, recovery of victims of Violence;
c. Rehabilitation, Reintegration and empowerment;
d. law enforcement services and legal aid;
e. facilitation of juvenile justice; and
f. cultivation of a gender-just social system.

