Children victims of Violence are Children who experience actions that result in misery or suffering physically, mentally, sexually, psychologically or neglect that threatens life, body and degrades human dignity;

Children in emergency situations as referred to are Children who become refugees, Children victims of riots and turmoil, Children victims of disasters and Children in conflict situations;

Children in disaster situations are natural disasters, fire disasters and riots;

Handling of complaints is a series of actions taken by integrated service providers to follow up on reports of acts of Violence against Women and Children submitted by victims, families or Society;

Social rehabilitation is services aimed at restoring and developing the ability of a person experiencing social dysfunction to be able to carry out social functions normally;

Social reintegration is an effort to reunite victims with family members, substitute families, or Society that can provide Protection and fulfill the needs of victims;

Integrated service unit or abbreviated as UPT is a unit that performs an integrated service function for Women and Children victims of Violence;

Safe house is a temporary shelter that aims to provide Protection and a sense of security to victims of Violence;

Child Protection Institution or abbreviated as LPA is an Independent Institution in the field of Child Protection and fulfillment of Children's rights that is community-based;

North Lombok Regency Integrated Service Center or abbreviated as PPT KLU is a form of integrated service implementation based on community health centers to handle victims of Violence against Women and Children which includes medical, medicolegal, and psychosocial services.

Article 26

(1) The Regional Government implements Integrated Services for Women and Children victims of acts of Violence through activities:

a. complaint services;
b. health services;
c. counseling;
d. spiritual guidance;
e. social Rehabilitation services;
f. legal assistance and Accompaniment services; and/or
g. repatriation and Reintegration.
(2) Services as referred to in paragraph (1) must be supported by facilities in the form of:
a. special service rooms within the police force;
b. expert and professional personnel;
c. service centers and safe houses; and/or
d. other facilities and infrastructure needed for victim recovery.
(3) The implementation of Services for victims of acts of Violence is carried out in an integrated manner by the Regional Government together with P2TP2A with other social institutions.
(4) P2TP2A and other social institutions as referred to in paragraph (3) may receive and send case referrals from other service units in a networked manner.
(5) Integrated Services for victims of acts of Violence as referred to in paragraphs (1) through (4) are implemented in accordance with Standard Operating Procedures.

Article 22

The Regional Government is responsible for efforts to protect Women and Children from acts of Violence that occur in the form of:

a. physical Violence;
b. sexual Violence;
c. economic Violence;
d. social Violence;
e. psychological Violence;
f. domestic neglect;
g. coercion or deprivation of freedom; and
h. threats of certain acts.

Article 16

(1) The relevant SKPD responsible for social affairs, health, and Protection of Women and Children, shall organize Handling and Recovery in the form of:

a. providing Assistance in legal processes;
b. conducting mediation and/or dispute resolution;
c. assisting with referrals, psychological and medical recovery;
d. assisting the legal identity process for Women and Children; and
e. conducting counseling.
(2) Implementation of Handling and Recovery as referred to in paragraph (1) may cooperate with the Police, Hospitals, Integrated Service Centers, Legal Aid Institutions, Business Entities and/or NGOs.

Article 24

(1) The Regional Government conducts prevention of Violence against Women and Children by means of:

a. socializing laws and regulations;
b. providing counseling/guidance;
c. providing education on the dangers of domestic Violence;
d. conducting seminars/workshops or the like;
e. forming work networks in efforts to prevent Violence;
f. conducting coordination, integration, synchronization of Violence prevention based on partnership patterns;
g. forming a Violence prevention system, mapping of locations or areas prone to the occurrence of Violence; and
h. increasing Society's awareness in behaving in accordance with religious norms and morality.
(2) In addition to the Regional Government, prevention as referred to in paragraph (1) must be implemented by:
a. family and/or closest relatives;
b. Society;
c. educational institutions;
d. health institutions;
e. social community institutions; and
f. the business world and other institutions.

Article 11

Every Child has the right to:

a. obtain education and teaching in accordance with age level, physical and mental condition, intelligence and interests and talents;
b. live, grow, develop and participate properly in accordance with human dignity and dignity, and receive Protection from acts of Violence, exploitation, discrimination and neglect;
c. have his/her needs fulfilled by the family;
d. receive religious guidance;
e. obtain his/her identity; and
f. obtain other rights in accordance with his/her human dignity and based on the provisions of laws and regulations.

